<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Chetumal</h1><p class="st-meta">1441 CE – 1544 CE (approx.) · capital Chetumal</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maya province on Chetumal Bay, rich in cacao, where the Spanish castaway Gonzalo Guerrero became a Maya war leader against his countrymen.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Chetumal (Chactemal) emerged as a powerful province after the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-mayapan">League of Mayapan</a> around 1441, on the bay shared today by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belize">Belize</a>. Its fertile lands produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a> and honey, and its towns were linked by trade to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras">Honduras</a> and the north.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Chetumal was ruled by the lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nachan-kaan">Nachan Kaan</a> at the time of the conquest. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-guerrero">Gonzalo Guerrero</a>, shipwrecked in 1511, married his daughter, adopted Maya customs and led its warriors against the Spanish; he died in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras">Honduras</a> around 1536. The province defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alonso-davila">Alonso Dávila's</a> attempt to found a settlement in 1531.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1544 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspar-pacheco">Gaspar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melchor-pacheco">Melchor Pacheco</a> conquered Chetumal brutally, and it was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-yucatan">Province of Yucatán</a>. The modern city of Chetumal, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintana-roo">Quintana Roo</a>, was founded in 1898.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chetumal.jpg" alt="Chetumal" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: AdriLov · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montaje_Chetumal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1441 CE – 1544 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chetumal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nachan Kaan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yucatec Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Mexico</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chactemal</dd></dl></aside></div>
